IMPORT prelude

-- Significant Investments Review Act 2024 (Singapore) -- who must notify, and who needs the Minister's prior approval, when buying
-- into or selling out of a designated entity: the controller thresholds (s 16), notice by a Level A controller and its defences
-- (s 18), prior approval (s 19), the entity's duty to report (s 20), void transactions (s 21(1)), approval of officers (s 27),
-- the two-year look-back over ANY entity (s 32(1)-(3)), the Part 3 penalties (s 36), and reconsideration before appeal (ss 38, 39).
--
-- Edition: Act No. 1 of 2024, informal consolidation (version in force from 28/3/2024), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SIRA2024.txt. The deposit annotates no amending Act or subsidiary legislation.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0079 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what an investor, a designated entity and its officers meet. Not encoded: administration and
-- delegation (Part 2), the meaning of "equity interest" (s 14) and "associate" (s 15) -- the encoding takes the person's
-- percentage, alone or with associates, as given -- designation itself (s 17) beyond who may be designated, remedial directions
-- (ss 22-25), winding-up restrictions (s 26), removal of officers (s 28) beyond its penalty, special administration (ss 29-31),
-- the directions and their effect (ss 32(5)-(9), 33), information powers (ss 34, 35, Part 5), the Reviewing Tribunal (ss 40-45),
-- and prescribed percentages other than the defaults in s 16(2) (no regulations were retrieved).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Significant Investments Review Act 2024 -- controllers`

-- A helper (the prelude has no max).
GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the higher of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT LEAST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `16 -- controller levels`

-- s 16(1): a "Level A controller" is a person who, "alone or together with the person's associates", (a) holds Level A% or more,
-- but less than Level B%, of the total equity interests, OR (b) is in a position to control Level A% or more, but less than
-- Level B%, of the voting power. Levels B, C and Y are bands in the same form; Levels D and Z have no upper limit.
-- s 16(2): unless another percentage is prescribed, Level A% is 5%, Level B% 12%, Level C% 25%, Level D% 50%, Level Y% 50% and
-- Level Z% 75%. Only these defaults are encoded.
--
-- The two limbs are alternatives, so a person holding 6% of the equity but controlling 13% of the votes is, on the words, BOTH a
-- Level A and a Level B controller.
GIVEN share IS A NUMBER, low IS A NUMBER, high IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the band` share low high IF
    share AT LEAST low AND share LESS THAN high

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level A controller` equity votes IF
    `in the band` equity 5 12 OR `in the band` votes 5 12

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level B controller` equity votes IF
    `in the band` equity 12 25 OR `in the band` votes 12 25

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level C controller` equity votes IF
    `in the band` equity 25 50 OR `in the band` votes 25 50

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level D controller` equity votes IF
    equity AT LEAST 50 OR votes AT LEAST 50

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level Y controller` equity votes IF
    `in the band` equity 50 75 OR `in the band` votes 50 75

GIVEN equity IS A NUMBER, votes IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a Level Z controller` equity votes IF
    equity AT LEAST 75 OR votes AT LEAST 75

-- For the duties below the encoding follows ONE percentage -- the person's equity and voting control taken as the same figure,
-- before and after a transaction. (A simplification: the Act tests each limb separately.)

§§ `18 -- notice by a Level A controller`

-- s 18(1): a person who becomes, on or after the designation date, a Level A controller "must, within 7 days after becoming the
-- Level A controller, give notice in writing to the Minister". (2) not if Level A% equals Level B%, C% or D% (not so on the
-- defaults). (3) contravention is an offence.
-- Because Level A is a band (5% up to 12%), a person who jumps from below 5% straight past 12% never becomes a Level A
-- controller: no s 18 notice is due, but s 19 approval is.
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER, after IS A NUMBER, `on or after the designation date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must notify the Minister as a Level A controller` IF
        `on or after the designation date`
    AND `is a Level A controller` after after
    AND (NOT `is a Level A controller` before before)

-- s 18(4): a defence to prove the accused "(a) was not aware of the contravention when it occurred; and (b) notified the Minister
-- ... within a period of 14 days after becoming aware". (5): also a defence, though aware, if (a) the contravention resulted from
-- an increase by an associate, (b) the accused has no agreement or arrangement with that associate about the interests or voting,
-- and (c) notified the Minister "within a period of 7 days after the contravention". (6): otherwise lack of intent or knowledge
-- is no defence.
GIVEN `was aware when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from awareness to notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `caused by an associate's increase` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days from contravention to notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a defence to the s 18 offence` IF
        ((NOT `was aware when it occurred`) AND `days from awareness to notice` AT MOST 14)
    OR  (`caused by an associate's increase` AND (NOT `has an arrangement with that associate`) AND `days from contravention to notice` AT MOST 7)

§§ `19 -- prior written approval of the Minister`

-- s 19(1): "Except with the prior written approval of the Minister, on or after the designation date -- (a) a person must not
-- become a Level B controller, Level C controller or Level D controller ...; and (b) a Level Y controller or Level Z controller
-- ... must not cease to be a Level Y controller or Level Z controller". (2): not if the transaction "is entered into before the
-- designation date".
--
-- On the words, a Level Y controller (50% to under 75%) who goes UP to 75% or more "ceases to be a Level Y controller", so needs
-- approval under (b) though (a) is not engaged (the person was already a Level D controller).
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER, after IS A NUMBER, `entered into before the designation date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `needs the Minister's prior approval` IF
        (NOT `entered into before the designation date`)
    AND (    (`is a Level B controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level B controller` before before))
         OR  (`is a Level C controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level C controller` before before))
         OR  (`is a Level D controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level D controller` before before))
         OR  (`is a Level Y controller` before before AND (NOT `is a Level Y controller` after after))
         OR  (`is a Level Z controller` before before AND (NOT `is a Level Z controller` after after)))

-- s 19(3): prior written approval to become an indirect controller; (4): to acquire, as a going concern, the business or
-- undertaking or any part of it. (10): contravening (1), (3) or (4), or any condition of approval, is an offence.
-- s 21(1): "A transaction that is completed in contravention of section 19(1), (3) or (4) is void" -- unless validated by a
-- validation notice (s 21(3), (7)).
GIVEN `approval was needed` IS A BOOLEAN, `prior written approval was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN, `a validation notice was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is void` IF
    `approval was needed` AND (NOT `prior written approval was obtained`) AND (NOT `a validation notice was issued`)

-- s 19(11): defence to a s 19(1) offence if the accused (a) was not aware when it occurred, (b) notified the Minister within 14 days
-- after becoming aware, and (c) complied with any s 22-24 direction in time, or the time has not expired. (12): or, though aware,
-- the contravention resulted from an associate's increase or decrease, there is no arrangement with the associate, the accused
-- "took all reasonable steps to notify the Minister ... within a period of 7 days after the contravention", and (d) as (c).
GIVEN `was aware when it occurred` IS A BOOLEAN, `days from awareness to notice` IS A NUMBER,
      `caused by an associate's change` IS A BOOLEAN, `has an arrangement with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took all reasonable steps to notify within 7 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `any direction complied with or still in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `has a defence to the s 19(1) offence` IF
        `any direction complied with or still in time`
    AND (    ((NOT `was aware when it occurred`) AND `days from awareness to notice` AT MOST 14)
         OR  (`caused by an associate's change` AND (NOT `has an arrangement with that associate`) AND `took all reasonable steps to notify within 7 days`))

§§ `20 -- the designated entity's duty to report`

-- s 20(1): a designated entity that becomes aware that, on or after the designation date, (a) a person has become a Level A, B, C
-- or D controller, (b) a Level Y or Z controller has ceased to be one, (c) a person has become an indirect controller, or (d) a
-- person has acquired the business or undertaking as a going concern, "must inform the Minister in writing within 7 days after
-- becoming aware of that fact". (2) offence.
GIVEN before IS A NUMBER, after IS A NUMBER, `someone became an indirect controller` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `someone acquired the business as a going concern` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the designated entity must inform the Minister` IF
        (`is a Level A controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level A controller` before before))
    OR  (`is a Level B controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level B controller` before before))
    OR  (`is a Level C controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level C controller` before before))
    OR  (`is a Level D controller` after after AND (NOT `is a Level D controller` before before))
    OR  (`is a Level Y controller` before before AND (NOT `is a Level Y controller` after after))
    OR  (`is a Level Z controller` before before AND (NOT `is a Level Z controller` after after))
    OR  `someone became an indirect controller`
    OR  `someone acquired the business as a going concern`

GIVEN `days since becoming aware` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity's report is in time` IF
    `days since becoming aware` AT MOST 7

§§ `27 -- approval of officers`

-- s 27(1): an individual may not be appointed as chief executive officer, director, or chairperson of the board of a designated
-- entity that is a corporation (or manager or partner of an LLP, or partner of a partnership) "without the Minister's approval upon
-- an application made by the designated entity". (5): an approved individual "may, without the Minister's approval, be
-- re-appointed ... immediately upon the expiry of the individual's term". (7): contravention without reasonable excuse is an
-- offence by the designated entity.
DECLARE Post IS ONE OF
    `chief executive officer`
    `director`
    `chairperson of the board`
    `company secretary`
    `ordinary employee`

GIVEN post IS A Post, `approved for this post before` IS A BOOLEAN, `re-appointment immediately on expiry of term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment needs the Minister's approval` IF
    CONSIDER post
    WHEN `company secretary` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `ordinary employee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT (`approved for this post before` AND `re-appointment immediately on expiry of term`)

§§ `32(1)-(3) -- the two-year look-back over any entity`

-- s 32(1): this section applies to ANY entity incorporated in Singapore, carrying out any activity in Singapore, or providing any
-- goods and services to any person in Singapore -- designated or not. (2): it applies if a person acquires or disposes of any
-- equity interest or voting control, becomes an indirect controller, or acquires the business, and the entity "has acted against
-- the national security interests of Singapore within a period of 2 years after the transaction". (3): the Minister may, "within a
-- period of 2 years and 30 days after the transaction", publish a review notice.
-- The encoding counts in days and takes 2 years as 730 days (an inference: the Act does not say how years are counted).
GIVEN `incorporated in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `carries out activity in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `supplies anyone in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity is within section 32` IF
    `incorporated in Singapore` OR `carries out activity in Singapore` OR `supplies anyone in Singapore`

GIVEN `days from transaction to the act against national security` IS A NUMBER, `days from transaction to the review notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a review notice may be published` IF
        `days from transaction to the act against national security` AT MOST 730
    AND `days from transaction to the review notice` AT MOST 760

§§ `36 -- penalties under Part 3`

-- s 36(1), for offences "for which no penalty is expressly provided": (a) an individual -- a fine not exceeding, for an offence
-- under s 18(3), 19(10), 20(2) or 21(11) (or s 32(8) by the person X), "the higher of ... the transaction value; $500,000", and
-- in any other case $500,000; or imprisonment up to 3 years, or both; continuing, a further $50,000 a day. (b) not an individual
-- -- for those listed offences, the higher of the transaction value and $1 million; in any other case "the higher of ... 10% of
-- the annual turnover of the offender's business; $1 million"; continuing, a further $100,000 a day.
-- (2)(b): turnover "is ascertained from the person's latest audited accounts". (3): the value of a void transaction is taken "as if
-- the transaction were not void".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `failing to notify as a Level A controller`
    `acting without the Minister's approval`
    `a designated entity failing to report`
    `breaching a condition of a validation notice`
    `the transacting person failing to comply with a section 32 direction`
    `another person failing to comply with a section 32 direction`
    `appointing an officer without approval`
    `failing to remove an officer as directed`

GIVEN offence IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fine is measured by the transaction value` IF
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `failing to notify as a Level A controller` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acting without the Minister's approval` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a designated entity failing to report` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `breaching a condition of a validation notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the transacting person failing to comply with a section 32 direction` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN offence IS AN Offence, `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN, `transaction value` IS A NUMBER, `annual turnover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` offence `is an individual` `transaction value` `annual turnover` MEANS
    IF `is an individual`
    THEN IF `the fine is measured by the transaction value` offence
         THEN `the higher of` `transaction value` 500000
         ELSE 500000
    ELSE IF `the fine is measured by the transaction value` offence
         THEN `the higher of` `transaction value` 1000000
         ELSE `the higher of` (`annual turnover` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100) 1000000

GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine for each day an offence continues` `is an individual` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 50000 ELSE 100000

-- s 36(1)(a)(ii): imprisonment "not exceeding 3 years" -- for individuals only.
GIVEN `is an individual` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` `is an individual` MEANS
    IF `is an individual` THEN 3 ELSE 0

§§ `38, 39 -- reconsideration before appeal`

-- s 38(2)(b): an application for reconsideration must be made "before the time specified in the initial appealable decision, being
-- a time that must not be later than the 14th day after the initial appealable decision was given". (7): the decision must be
-- complied with meanwhile. s 39(2): "No appeal may be made ... to a Reviewing Tribunal unless the appellant has first applied
-- under section 38(1)" and the Minister has substituted or affirmed the decision. s 46: decisions are final and not to be
-- challenged in court except on compliance with procedural requirements.
GIVEN `days after the decision was given` IS A NUMBER, `days allowed by the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reconsideration application is in time` IF
        `days after the decision was given` AT MOST `days allowed by the decision`
    AND `days after the decision was given` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `applied for reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister affirmed or substituted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may appeal to a Reviewing Tribunal` IF
    `applied for reconsideration` AND `the Minister affirmed or substituted`
